<h1>tournament</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Find the maximum of a set of n elements in  &lceil;log n&rceil; "rounds" (passes) by "playing" (comparing) pairs of elements and advancing the winner (greater) of each pair to the next round.  It takes n-1 comparisons, like <a href="linearSearch.html"><em>linear search</em></a>, but may be parallelized, extended to also find the second greatest element, etc.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="selectkth.html"><em>select k<sup>th</sup> element</em></a>, <a href="selectAndPartition.html"><em>select and partition</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The second greatest element can be found with log n - 1 additional comparisons.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorGS">GS</a></p>

